<section class="section faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="faq-header">
      <div class="feature-kicker">Learn more</div>
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>How is Octavise different from Meta or Google Ads reporting?</summary>
        <p>Meta and Google show ad-platform activity. Octavise adds practice context: bookings, new patients, revenue, cancellations, referrals, and operating trends.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which systems does Octavise connect to?</summary>
        <p>Octavise currently supports Nookal and Cliniko for practice management, plus Meta Ads and Google Ads for advertising data.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is this exact patient-level attribution?</summary>
        <p>No. Octavise is designed to show practical performance context and correlation, not overclaim deterministic patient-level attribution.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does Octavise modify campaigns or practice records?</summary>
        <p>No. The dashboard uses read-only access and does not change appointments, patient records, or ad campaigns.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does the founder offer include?</summary>
        <p>The offer gives early practices 30% off with the code FOUNDER30 while the first 10 founder spots are available.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
